}
```
Reason:
This code incorrectly restricts the TLS TX device offload feature to only be enabled when the NETIF_F_HW_CSUM feature is set. As a result, devices that support IP_CSUM and IPV6_CSUM are unable to utilize the TLS TX offload, leading to functionality issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
bool ip_csum = (features & (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM)) ==
    (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM);
bool hw_csum = features & NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;

if (!ip_csum && !hw_csum) {
    netdev_dbg(dev, "Dropping TLS TX HW offload feature since no CSUM feature.\n");
    features &= ~NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check to determine if either IP_CSUM or IPV6_CSUM is set, allowing the TLS TX offload feature to remain enabled if either of these checksum features is present, rather than solely relying on HW_CSUM. This ensures that devices supporting IP_CSUM and IPV6_CSUM can utilize the TLS TX offload functionality correctly.

